<body>
    <div class="container">
        <header class="header">
            <div class="heading-container">
                <h1 class="heading">The DISC</h1>
                <h1 class="heading">Personality Test</h1>
            </div>
            <div class="result" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                <h4>
                    RESULTS FOR: <b>
                        <%= answer.user_name %>
                    </b>
                </h4>
                <!-- <p class="description" style="font-size: 12px;">Jan 18, 2021 -8:37AM</p> -->
                <p class="description" style="font-size: 12px;">
                    <%= answer.formattedDate %>
                </p>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div style="margin: 10px 50px 50px 50px;">
            <div>
                <!-- Section 1. -->
                <section>
                    <h3 class="vertical-space">
                        About DISC:
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        DISC is a widely-used behavioral assessment tool that categorizes human behavior into four
                        primary
                        personality traits: Dominance (D), Influence (I), Steadiness (S), and Conscientiousness (C).
                        Developed based on the work of psychologist William Moulton Marston, the DISC model helps
                        individuals gain insights into their communication styles, behavioral tendencies, and
                        interaction
                        preferences.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        By understanding their DISC profile, individuals can enhance self-awareness, improve
                        communication
                        with others, and adapt their approach in various personal and professional situations.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        DISC assessments are commonly used for personal development, team building, leadership training,
                        and
                        conflict resolution.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The DISC model is frequently depicted through a visual representation showcasing the four
                        personality types positioned within four quadrants of a circular framework.
                    </p>

                    <img src="<%= answer['disc1img'] %>" style="width: 100%; height: 100%" alt="disc1img" />

                    <p>
                        The graphic illustrates the DISC model through two primary axes: Outgoing vs. Reserved
                        vertically and Task-oriented vs. People-oriented horizontally. These axes represent the
                        foundational styles assessed by the DISC system, determining your position within the graph.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="vertical-space">DISC fundamentals</h3>
                    <p>
                        At the core of DISC lies its fundamental dimensions, which serve as the cornerstone of
                        personality assessment. These dimensions are the primary drivers of individual behavior, shaping
                        communication styles and interaction preferences. By examining the combination of scores on
                        these two dimensions, DISC provides a comprehensive understanding of an individual's personality
                        profile, illuminating their unique blend of traits and tendencies.
                    </p>

                    <h4 class="top-extra-space">The first axis OUTGOING VS RESERVED</h4>
                    <p>
                        The first axis in the DISC model, Outgoing vs. Reserved, represents a fundamental dimension of
                        personality related to social interaction.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Individuals positioned towards the outgoing end of this axis are characterized by traits such as
                        sociability, assertiveness, and a preference for engaging with others. They tend to be outgoing,
                        expressive, and comfortable in social settings.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        On the other hand, individuals positioned towards the reserved end of this axis exhibit traits
                        such as introversion, caution, and a preference for solitude or smaller social gatherings. They
                        may be more reflective, observant, and reserved in their interactions with others.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The Outgoing vs. Reserved axis captures the spectrum of social behavior and communication
                        styles, highlighting the diversity of personality traits related to social interaction
                        preferences.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Understanding where individuals fall along this axis provides insights into their comfort level
                        in social situations, communication style, and approach to interpersonal relationships.
                    </p>

                    <h4 class="top-extra-space">The second axis PEOPLE-ORIENTED vs TASK-ORIENTED</h4>
                    <p>
                        The second axis in the DISC model, people-oriented vs. task-oriented, represents another
                        foundational dimension of personality related to goal pursuit and interpersonal dynamics.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Individuals positioned towards the people-oriented end of this axis prioritize relationships,
                        collaboration, and the well-being of others. They are often empathetic, supportive, and enjoy
                        working closely with others to achieve common goals. People-oriented individuals excel in roles
                        that require teamwork, communication, and building rapport.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        On the other hand, individuals positioned towards the task-oriented end of this axis prioritize
                        efficiency, productivity, and achieving tangible outcomes. They are focused on completing tasks,
                        solving problems, and meeting objectives. Task-oriented individuals are often organized,
                        detail-oriented, and thrive in environments where clear goals and deadlines are set.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The people-oriented vs. task-oriented axis captures the balance between focusing on
                        relationships and focusing on tasks in one's approach to work and interactions with others.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Understanding where individuals fall along this axis provides insights into their preferred work
                        style, communication preferences, and contributions to team dynamics.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 2. -->
                <section>
                    <h3 class="vertical-space">Your scores on the two dimensions</h3>
                    <h4 class="bottom-extra-space">The OUTGOING-RESERVED axis</h4>
                    <div class="progress-container content-breck">
                        <div class="first left-one">
                            <span style="margin-right: 15px; font-weight: 600;">RESERVED
                                <%=answer.Reserved_percentage %>%
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="second right-one">
                            <span style="margin-left: 15px; font-weight: 600;">OUTGOING
                                <%=answer.Outgoing_percentage %>%
                            </span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <%if(answer.Reserved_percentage>60){%>
                            <p>
                                You are on the RESERVED side of the axis so you find comfort in quieter, more intimate
                                settings, preferring meaningful connections within a close circle of friends. While you
                                may not seek out social interactions as frequently as others, your reflective nature
                                allows you to bring depth and insight to conversations. In group settings, you
                                contribute thoughtfully, taking your time to process information before sharing your
                                thoughts.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Your reserved demeanor lends itself well to roles that require focused attention and
                                thoughtful consideration, allowing you to excel in environments where depth and insight
                                are valued.
                            </p>
                            <% } %>
                                <%if(answer.Outgoing_percentage>60){%>
                                    <p>
                                        You are on OUTGOING side of this dimension so you excel in social environments,
                                        demonstrating a natural inclination towards interaction and taking the
                                        initiative in conversations and group activities.
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        Your outgoing nature allows you to connect easily with others, and you often
                                        find yourself energized by social engagement, thriving in situations where
                                        collaboration and communication are key.
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        Your assertiveness and comfort in social settings make you a valuable
                                        contributor to group dynamics, and you're often seen as a natural leader who can
                                        inspire and motivate those around you.
                                    </p>
                                    <% } %>
                                        <% if ((answer.Reserved_percentage < 60 && answer.Reserved_percentage> 40) ||
                                            (answer.Outgoing_percentage < 60 && answer.Outgoing_percentage> 40)) { %>
                                                <p>
                                                    You scored in the middle of this dimension so you possess a balanced
                                                    approach to social interactions, feeling at ease in both larger
                                                    gatherings and intimate conversations.
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                    Your adaptability allows you to engage confidently when necessary,
                                                    while
                                                    also appreciating moments of solitude and reflection. In group
                                                    settings,
                                                    you navigate dynamics effectively, contributing insights while
                                                    listening
                                                    attentively to others.
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                    Your versatility enables you to connect with a diverse range of
                                                    individuals, thriving in various social and professional contexts.
                                                </p>
                                                <% } %>
                    </div>

                    <h4 class="vertical-space">The PEOPLE-ORIENTED – TASK-ORIENTED axis</h4>
                    <div class="progress-container content-breck">
                        <div class="first left-two">
                            <span style="margin-right: 15px; font-weight: 600;">TASK-ORIENTED
                                <%=answer.TaskOriented_percentage %>%
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="second right-two">
                            <span style="margin-left: 15px; font-weight: 600;">PEOPLE-ORIENTED
                                <%=answer.PeopleOriented_percentage %>%
                            </span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <%if(answer.TaskOriented_percentage>60){%>
                            <p>
                                You are on TASK-ORIENTED side of this dimension so you prioritize efficiency and
                                productivity, excelling in environments where clear goals and deadlines are set.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                You are focused on completing tasks and achieving tangible outcomes, often
                                demonstrating strong organizational skills and attention to detail.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Your ability to stay on track and meet objectives ensures that projects are
                                completed successfully and goals are reached effectively.
                            </p>
                            <% } %>

                                <%if(answer.PeopleOriented_percentage>60){%>
                                    <p>
                                        You are on the PEOPLE-ORIENTED side of this dimension so you prioritize relationships
                                        and collaboration, thriving in environments where teamwork and communication are key.
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        You excel at building rapport and supporting others, valuing interpersonal connections
                                        above all else.
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        Your empathetic nature allows you to understand the needs of those around you, fostering
                                        a positive and supportive atmosphere in both personal and professional settings.
                                    </p>
                                    <% } %>

                                        <% if ((answer.TaskOriented_percentage < 60 && answer.TaskOriented_percentage>
                                            40) || (answer.PeopleOriented_percentage < 60 &&
                                                answer.PeopleOriented_percentage> 40)) { %>
                                                <p>
                                                    You scored in the middle of this dimension meaning that you possess
                                                    a
                                                    balanced approach between being PEOPLE-ORIENTED and TASK-ORIENTED.
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                    You value both building relationships and achieving tangible
                                                    outcomes.
                                                    This allows you to effectively collaborate with others while also
                                                    ensuring tasks are completed efficiently.
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                    Your ability to prioritize both people and tasks contributes to your
                                                    success in various endeavors, fostering strong relationships and
                                                    achieving goals effectively.
                                                </p>
                                                <% } %>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 3. -->
                <section>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="vertical-space">Putting your scores on the two dimensions together</h3>
                        <p>
                            The DISC assessment measures the combined dimensions that shape your personality type. In
                            the DISC circle, the OUTGOING - RESERVED dimension is mapped from top to bottom, while the
                            TASK-ORIENTED - PEOPLE-ORIENTED dimension is mapped from left to right. These two axes
                            intersect, creating four quadrants, each representing a distinct personality type. Your
                            individual scores may fall anywhere within the circle, indicating your unique blend of
                            traits and tendencies.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 4. -->
                <section>
                    <div>
                        <%if(answer.Quadrant=='I_type'){%>
                            <p>
                                Your scores on the OUTGOING side as well as on the PEOPLE-ORIENTED side puts your
                                overall result into the I quadrant. This indicates that INFLUENCE is the most dominant
                                style for you.
                            </p>
                            <img src="<%= answer['disc3img'] %>" style="width: 100%; height: 100%" alt="disc3img" />
                            <% } %>

                                <%if(answer.Quadrant=='S_type'){%>
                                    <p>
                                        Your scores on the RESERVED side as well as on the PEOPLE-ORIENTED side puts
                                        your overall result into the S quadrant. This indicates that STEADINESS is the
                                        most dominant style for you.
                                    </p>
                                    <img src="<%= answer['disc5img'] %>" style="width: 100%; height: 100%"
                                        alt="disc5img" />
                                    <% } %>

                                        <%if(answer.Quadrant=='C_type'){%>
                                            <p>
                                                Your scores on the RESERVED side as well as on the TASK-ORIENTED side
                                                puts your overall result into the C quadrant. This indicates that
                                                CONSCIENTIOUSNSS is the most dominant style for you.
                                            </p>
                                            <img src="<%= answer['disc4img'] %>" style="width: 100%; height: 100%"
                                                alt="disc4img" />
                                            <% } %>

                                                <%if(answer.Quadrant=='D_type'){%>
                                                    <p>
                                                        Your scores on the OUTGOING side as well as on the TASK-ORIENTED
                                                        side puts your overall result into the D quadrant. This
                                                        indicates that DOMINANCE is the most dominant style for you.
                                                    </p>
                                                    <img src="<%= answer['disc2img'] %>"
                                                        style="width: 100%; height: 100%" alt="disc2img" />
                                                    <% } %>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 5. -->
                <section>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="vertical-space">Exploring DISC types further</h3>
                        <p>
                            The visual representation provided offers an overview of your scores, yet the DISC system
                            offers additional depth.
                        </p>
                        <h4 class="vertical-space">About the main DISC types</h4>
                        <p>
                            <span class="bold-text">Dominance – D :</span>
                            Individuals with Dominance as their primary DISC type tend to exhibit assertive, decisive,
                            and results-oriented behavior. They are often seen as natural leaders who take charge in
                            challenging situations and are unafraid to make tough decisions. Dominant individuals are
                            driven by goals and enjoy taking on challenges, thriving in environments where they can
                            assert their authority and drive towards success. They are typically direct communicators
                            who value efficiency and effectiveness, preferring to focus on the big picture rather than
                            getting bogged down in details. While their assertiveness and determination can be assets,
                            Dominant individuals may need to be mindful of balancing their leadership style with empathy
                            and consideration for others' perspectives.
                        </p>

                        <p class="top-extra-space">
                            <span class="bold-text">Influence – I :</span>
                            Individuals with Influence as their primary DISC type are typically outgoing, sociable, and
                            charismatic. They thrive in social settings and enjoy being the center of attention.
                            Influential individuals are natural communicators who excel at building relationships and
                            motivating others. They are often seen as enthusiastic and optimistic, bringing energy and
                            positivity to any situation. Influencers are creative thinkers who enjoy brainstorming and
                            exploring new ideas. They are adept at persuasion and are skilled at navigating social
                            dynamics to achieve their goals. While their sociability and charm can be advantageous,
                            Influence types may need to be mindful of balancing their desire for social interaction with
                            the need for focus and follow-through on tasks.
                        </p>

                        <p class="top-extra-space">
                            <span class="bold-text">Steadiness – S :</span>
                            Individuals with Steadiness as their primary DISC type are characterized by their stability,
                            patience, and supportive nature. They value harmony and prefer to work in environments where
                            they feel secure and appreciated. Steadiness types are reliable team players who prioritize
                            loyalty and cooperation. They are often empathetic listeners who offer emotional support to
                            others and foster a sense of unity within groups. Steady individuals are known for their
                            calm demeanor and ability to remain composed under pressure. They excel in roles that
                            require attention to detail and consistency, as they are thorough and methodical in their
                            approach to tasks. While their steady and supportive nature is an asset to team dynamics,
                            Steadiness types may need to be mindful of assertiveness and advocating for their own needs
                            in order to avoid being overlooked or taken advantage of.
                        </p>

                        <p class="top-extra-space">
                            <span class="bold-text">Conscientiousness – C :</span>
                            Individuals with Conscientiousness as their primary DISC type are known for their analytical
                            thinking, attention to detail, and organized approach to tasks. They prioritize accuracy and
                            precision in their work and are committed to upholding high standards of quality.
                            Conscientious types are diligent and systematic in their planning and execution, often
                            taking a methodical approach to problem-solving. They are reliable and responsible
                            individuals who take their commitments seriously and strive for excellence in everything
                            they do.
                        </p>

                        <div class="top-extra-space">
                            <p>
                                Beyond identifying your primary type, we can precisely map your scores within the
                                circle, providing a comprehensive understanding of your behavioral style. Let's explore
                                a detailed graph of your scores across the DISC framework for a more nuanced
                                perspective.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                The following graph presents a variation from the previous one. While you'll still
                                recognize the familiar initials of D, I, S, and C, you'll notice that there are now
                                twelve chart segments instead of four. Additionally, some segments are labeled with
                                combinations like I/d or S/i. These hybrid DISC types represent blends of styles,
                                offering a more nuanced understanding of behavioral tendencies. For example, someone who
                                primarily exhibits Influence traits but also incorporates elements of Dominance behavior
                                in their work style would be labeled an I/d type. These hybrid styles enhance the
                                descriptive power of the system, accurately capturing individuals whose behavior is
                                primarily driven by one DISC style, as well as those who exhibit a mix of two styles.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                The chart below illustrates your scores within the detailed DISC circle. Larger segments
                                represent higher scores for each type.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 6. -->
                <section>
                    <div>
                        <%if(answer.UTypeOne=='ID'){%>
                            <p class="bold-text vertical-space">Your DISC type is Influence/Dominance !</p>
                            <p>
                                Individuals with a hybrid <span class="bold-text">Influence/Dominance</span> DISC style
                                often exhibit a unique blend of
                                traits from both the Influence and Dominance styles. They are typically outgoing,
                                sociable, and charismatic, with a natural ability to connect with others and influence
                                their opinions. At the same time, they possess assertiveness, confidence, and a strong
                                desire to take charge and lead others towards their goals.
                            </p>
                            <% } %>
                                <%if(answer.UTypeOne=='I'){%>
                                    <p class="bold-text vertical-space">Your DISC type is Influence !</p>
                                    <p>
                                        Individuals with an <span class="bold-text">Influence</span> DISC style are
                                        characterized by their sociability,
                                        enthusiasm, and natural ability to connect with others. They are often outgoing
                                        and charismatic, with a talent for building relationships and inspiring those
                                        around them. These individuals excel in roles that require persuasion,
                                        communication, and creativity, often serving as natural leaders who can rally
                                        teams towards a shared vision.
                                    </p>
                                    <% } %>
                                        <%if(answer.UTypeOne=='IS'){%>
                                            <p class="bold-text vertical-space">Your DISC type is Influence/Steadiness !
                                            </p>
                                            <p>
                                                Individuals with a hybrid <span
                                                    class="bold-text">Influence/Steadiness</span> DISC style possess a
                                                unique combination of traits from both the Influence and Steadiness
                                                styles. They are often sociable, outgoing, and energetic, enjoying
                                                interactions with others and seeking to build positive relationships. At
                                                the same time, they also exhibit qualities such as patience,
                                                reliability, and a desire for stability and harmony in their
